\tag{algorithms}
\taxon{Example}

\import{algorithms-macros}

\p{Consider #{T(n) = 3n^2 + 17n + 8}.  To show that this is #{O(n^2)} according to the definition, we can reason as follows:

  ##{\begin{align*}
    T(n) &= 3n^2 + 17n + 8 \\
         &\leq 3n^2 + 17n^2 + 8n^2 \quad (n \geq 1) \\
         &= 28n^2
  \end{align*}}

  So we can choose #{c = 28} and #{n_0 = 1}, which satisfies the definition, so #{T(n)} is #{O(n^2)}. (In fact we could also pick #{c = 4} along with a bigger #{n_0}.)}
